# Deterministic line endings for every clone, independent of the local
# core.autocrlf setting. Git for Windows defaults autocrlf=true, which
# made essentially every commit in this repo emit "LF will be replaced
# by CRLF" warnings. Normalizing here settles it in-tree, so it travels
# with the repo instead of depending on each developer's config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The committed ROMs are build output. They must never be considered
# text: any line-ending substitution would silently corrupt a binary
# that people flash to hardware.
*.nds binary
*.dsi binary

# build.bat is intentionally covered by the eol=lf rule above rather
# than forced to CRLF. cmd.exe reads LF batch files correctly, it is
# already LF in-tree, and it has been verified to run that way.
